{"In handleCancelBooking.ts, forEach is used to invoke async deleteScheduledEmailReminder and deleteScheduledSMSReminder without awaiting the returned promises. If the DB update to set cancelled=true fails, the error is silently swallowed and the reminder stays uncancelled, meaning the email will still be sent for a cancelled booking.": 0.9068962335586548, "In deleteScheduledEmailReminder, when immediateDelete=true and referenceId is present, the function sends a cancel request to SendGrid but returns without deleting the workflowReminder DB record or marking it as cancelled=true. These orphaned records won't be caught by the CRON's cancelled-reminder query and will linger in the database.": 0.9598050713539124, "scheduleEmailReminders selects reminders to cancel without filtering to EMAIL or ensuring referenceId is non-null, then sends reminder.referenceId to SendGrid as batch_id. This can attempt to cancel non-email reminders or reminders missing a referenceId, causing SendGrid request failures and leaving reminders uncancelled.": 0.9843915700912476, "In scheduleEmailReminders.ts, the entire cancellation loop is wrapped in a single try/catch. If any client.request() call throws, the catch block fires and Promise.all(workflowRemindersToDelete) is never awaited, so all previously accumulated Prisma delete promises are silently dropped.": 0.992965817451477, "The unscheduledReminders query in scheduleEmailReminders.ts fetches reminders with scheduled=false but does NOT exclude reminders with cancelled=true. A reminder that was cancelled before being scheduled will be picked up and scheduled via SendGrid, sending an unwanted email.": 0.9857391715049744}